# Local runtime authorization gate

Full policy: [`docs/guides/local-runtime-authorization.md`](../../docs/guides/local-runtime-authorization.md)

## Canonical order (do not skip)

1. Inspect → 2. Audit → 3. Task gate → 4. **Unit tests green** → **4b. `pre-push-check.sh`** → 5. Infra gate (if live needed) → 6. Live proof → 7. Commit-ready → 8. Commit (owner asks) → **9. Monitor GitHub CI**

**Never** request infra before step 4 passes. **Never** commit/push before step 4b passes. **Never** declare PR green without step 9.

## Three gates

| Gate | Trigger | After |
| ---- | ------- | ----- |
| Task | `ok` / `prossegue` | Inspect/plan accepted |
| Infra | `ok infra` | `./mvnw checkstyle:check test` + `pre-push-check.sh` BUILD SUCCESS |
| Commit | owner explicitly asks | Steps 4–6 green for scope |

## Pre-push (step 4b)

```bash
bash scripts/pre-push-check.sh
```

Mirrors CI `quality` job. Required before every commit/push when Java/XML changed.

## Post-push (step 9)

```bash
gh pr checks --watch
```

Fix and re-push on Maven CI failure. Report Sonar/GitGuardian separately.

## Commit-ready ≠ commit

Report "pronto para commitar" with checklist; wait for explicit owner commit request.
